- I can't think of one at
this point because I'm 87

01:05:36.384 --> 01:05:37.390
(audience laughing)

01:05:37.390 --> 01:05:42.390
so there used to be some but not anymore.

01:05:44.530 --> 01:05:49.530
No I got a chance and I've done
it everything I want to do.

01:05:50.000 --> 01:05:55.000
I'm working on my game,
Quiltuduko and if you know Sudoku,

01:05:56.870 --> 01:05:58.270
how many people know Sudoku?

01:05:59.320 --> 01:06:01.360
Well Quiltuduko is a lot like it.

01:06:01.360 --> 01:06:05.870
You just go on iTunes

01:06:07.380 --> 01:06:10.380
and what's the other Google Play

01:06:11.420 --> 01:06:14.697
and type in Quiltuduko

01:06:16.140 --> 01:06:20.993
Q-U-I-L-T-U-D-U-K-O

01:06:23.850 --> 01:06:25.603
and you can play my game.

01:06:26.527 --> 01:06:27.570
(audience laughing)

01:06:27.570 --> 01:06:32.410
It's so fun because with
Sudoku when you get finished,

01:06:32.410 --> 01:06:36.570
the only thing you've got are 81 numbers

01:06:38.410 --> 01:06:40.390
and you throw that paper out.

01:06:40.390 --> 01:06:43.270
But with Quiltuduko you've
got a poster you can put

01:06:43.270 --> 01:06:46.603
on the wall okay.

01:06:47.950 --> 01:06:49.333
It's gonna be fun.

01:06:56.050 --> 01:06:58.400
- [Woman] What's your
favorite thing about art?

01:07:01.290 --> 01:07:04.130
- I like the power of creativity

01:07:05.200 --> 01:07:10.200
that I am able to create something
out of my own imagination

01:07:13.080 --> 01:07:16.883
that has never been done before by me.

01:07:20.430 --> 01:07:22.140
That's what I like about it.

01:07:22.140 --> 01:07:27.140
It gives you a feeling of
power that is very memorable.

01:07:30.700 --> 01:07:32.023
I love creating art.

01:07:33.720 --> 01:07:35.657
And I love my art.

01:07:37.320 --> 01:07:38.830
Yeah I do.

01:07:38.830 --> 01:07:39.663
I love it.

01:07:40.550 --> 01:07:43.140
I don't try to please
other people with my art.

01:07:43.140 --> 01:07:45.960
I'm happy when they are pleased

01:07:45.960 --> 01:07:48.900
but as an artist I think it's important

01:07:48.900 --> 01:07:50.410
that you love what you're doing.

01:07:50.410 --> 01:07:55.163
You love it because you have
no idea what other people want.

01:07:59.741 --> 01:08:00.574
Okay.

01:08:08.700 --> 01:08:11.230
- [Woman] Thank you for the pleasure.

01:08:11.230 --> 01:08:14.620
An afternoon of beautiful, beautiful work.

01:08:14.620 --> 01:08:15.870
- Thank you.

01:08:15.870 --> 01:08:19.680
- [Woman] Well I want to
ask a very serious question

01:08:19.680 --> 01:08:21.350
at this time.
- Okay.

01:08:21.350 --> 01:08:26.350
- [Woman] Because as a nation
we are in deep, deep trouble

01:08:28.770 --> 01:08:33.650
and I wonder if you think
that replacing the arts

01:08:33.650 --> 01:08:38.650
in the curriculum will help
reduce school shootings.

01:08:38.840 --> 01:08:39.730
- Re-what?

01:08:39.730 --> 01:08:42.287
Replacing the art in the curriculum?

01:08:42.287 --> 01:08:43.120
With?

01:08:43.120 --> 01:08:44.003
- [Woman] Putting art back.

01:08:44.940 --> 01:08:49.118
- Oh, putting the art back
into, oh that's interesting.

01:08:49.118 --> 01:08:53.820
I'm wondering if children
are losing their sensibility.

01:08:53.820 --> 01:08:55.763
Their what?

01:08:59.086 --> 01:09:00.370
Do you think that's the reason

01:09:00.370 --> 01:09:01.970
why they're shooting each other?

01:09:03.160 --> 01:09:04.880
- [Woman] And their love for themselves.

01:09:04.880 --> 01:09:08.000
- And love, yes, for humanity,

01:09:08.000 --> 01:09:10.230
for the world, for creativity,

01:09:10.230 --> 01:09:15.230
for yeah, I don't know,

01:09:15.390 --> 01:09:19.403
is the art out of the schools
completely at this point?

01:09:20.582 --> 01:09:22.087
- It's coming out.
- It's coming out.

01:09:22.087 --> 01:09:23.987
It's going down though, right?
- Yes.

01:09:25.000 --> 01:09:29.510
- Unfortunately, you know
children have such an ability

01:09:29.510 --> 01:09:32.780
to create art when they're little.

01:09:32.780 --> 01:09:37.780
And to be denied that
opportunity is sinful.

01:09:40.480 --> 01:09:43.160
So that if they don't get it in school

01:09:43.160 --> 01:09:45.790
as parents you have to make
sure they get it at home

01:09:45.790 --> 01:09:50.613
because it's in them.

01:09:53.280 --> 01:09:55.957
I know they're not
getting the music either,

01:09:55.957 --> 01:09:58.107
huh they're not getting the music.

01:09:58.107 --> 01:10:01.065
- They are.
- They are getting the music?

01:10:01.065 --> 01:10:02.010
- [Woman] Now as the curriculum standing.

01:10:02.010 --> 01:10:03.560
- Okay, okay.

01:10:03.560 --> 01:10:05.306
- [Woman] Part of mandate.

01:10:05.306 --> 01:10:08.420
- Okay, well what can I say

01:10:11.250 --> 01:10:12.723
that's unfortunate,

01:10:15.000 --> 01:10:19.560
if they are being denied
the ability to be creative

01:10:20.510 --> 01:10:22.453
and to tell their story.

01:10:31.200 --> 01:10:32.380
- [Woman] I wasn't going to speak

01:10:32.380 --> 01:10:34.573
but I'm very compelled right now.

01:10:35.857 --> 01:10:36.690
I'm an art teacher

01:10:36.690 --> 01:10:39.310
and I'm a survivor of the
Sandy Hook School Shooting

01:10:40.530 --> 01:10:44.590
and five years ago I got
to meet Faith Ringgold

01:10:46.220 --> 01:10:51.220
and she validated so much
of what I had experienced.

01:10:52.330 --> 01:10:56.460
And I came to her because it was Tar Beach

01:10:57.670 --> 01:11:02.670
that allowed my students
to fly above the pain

01:11:04.250 --> 01:11:07.560
and the horror and I can't say enough

01:11:07.560 --> 01:11:10.660
about how you have influenced,

01:11:10.660 --> 01:11:15.350
to this day you are
influencing children's idea

01:11:15.350 --> 01:11:20.350
of what it is to create
and to be and to fly

01:11:21.120 --> 01:11:24.310
and I can't thank you enough for that.

01:11:24.310 --> 01:11:27.044
I'm humbled.
- Well thank you.

01:11:27.044 --> 01:11:30.294
(audience applauding)

01:11:31.691 --> 01:11:32.524
Yes.

01:11:34.830 --> 01:11:38.923
Yes, anyone can fly all,
you got to do is try.

01:11:40.790 --> 01:11:41.623
That's right.

01:11:43.000 --> 01:11:45.000
Thank you very much for telling me that.

01:11:48.160 --> 01:11:51.810
- [Man] Yeah so I guess as someone who now

01:11:51.810 --> 01:11:56.130
for a very long time has
not only been a part of

01:11:56.130 --> 01:12:00.500
but shaped conversations on
race and gender and belonging,

01:12:00.500 --> 01:12:03.080
I think a couple of people
have commented on the fact

01:12:03.080 --> 01:12:07.010
that in, certainly in America,

01:12:07.010 --> 01:12:08.750
but I think the the world in general

01:12:08.750 --> 01:12:12.230
it has I mean you know
they've never had its way

01:12:12.230 --> 01:12:14.850
to begin with but is
certainly more wayward

01:12:14.850 --> 01:12:16.323
than it's been in a while.

01:12:17.160 --> 01:12:20.900
And I'm wondering what you have to share

01:12:23.970 --> 01:12:27.380
about being in the center
of that conversation

01:12:27.380 --> 01:12:31.693
for a world which doesn't want
to be having it right now.

01:12:33.460 --> 01:12:37.120
- Well you just have to be forceful

01:12:37.120 --> 01:12:40.950
and find ways that are unique to you

01:12:42.110 --> 01:12:46.210
to bring love and truth

01:12:47.280 --> 01:12:51.403
into the world and
especially to the children.

01:12:52.360 --> 01:12:57.360
They have a right to embrace the world.

01:12:59.520 --> 01:13:04.520
As children they need to
have the world open to them

01:13:06.270 --> 01:13:11.270
to have opportunity to
learn and without it,

01:13:11.400 --> 01:13:13.410
oh my God that is so awful.

01:13:13.410 --> 01:13:18.090
I can't imagine how it must be

01:13:18.090 --> 01:13:23.090
to not be able to see the world

01:13:24.630 --> 01:13:27.373
as so many of us have taken for granted.

01:13:30.790 --> 01:13:32.040
Because as you get older,

01:13:32.040 --> 01:13:34.600
you're gonna become more and more aware

01:13:34.600 --> 01:13:35.993
of what you have missed.

01:13:39.190 --> 01:13:40.943
Let's hope it doesn't continue.

01:13:42.600 --> 01:13:45.160
But we have to do something about it

01:13:45.160 --> 01:13:48.570
and I would think that one
thing we could do is get rid

01:13:48.570 --> 01:13:51.236
of what's going on at the White House.

01:13:51.236 --> 01:13:54.486
(audience applauding)

01:13:57.480 --> 01:13:59.580
Yeah I mean the children can't do that.

01:13:59.580 --> 01:14:01.720
Somebody's got to do it.

01:14:01.720 --> 01:14:03.840
And you know how unfortunate,

01:14:03.840 --> 01:14:06.280
I mean I just think about how I would feel

01:14:07.369 --> 01:14:09.170
if as a child I had had somebody

01:14:10.010 --> 01:14:11.440
in the White House like that.

01:14:11.440 --> 01:14:13.440
It must be horrible just think about it.

01:14:17.230 --> 01:14:21.070
So we can change it
though if we get together,

01:14:21.070 --> 01:14:21.903
we can do it.

01:14:23.810 --> 01:14:24.643
I think so.

01:14:27.115 --> 01:14:28.388
Do you agree?

01:14:28.388 --> 01:14:29.635
- [Audience] Yes.

01:14:29.635 --> 01:14:32.289
(audience applauding)

01:14:32.289 --> 01:14:34.456
- All right, anybody else?

01:14:39.370 --> 01:14:40.604
Yes.

01:14:40.604 --> 01:14:41.770
- [Woman] Can I impose on you.

01:14:41.770 --> 01:14:45.140
I would like for you to
autograph a book of yours.

01:14:45.140 --> 01:14:48.140
(people chattering)

01:14:55.238 --> 01:14:56.071
- Yeah.

01:14:57.550 --> 01:14:59.480
- So I would liked

01:14:59.480 --> 01:15:02.976
to once more thank the
wonderful Faith Ringgold.

01:15:02.976 --> 01:15:05.574
(audience applauding)

01:15:05.574 --> 01:15:06.574
- Thank you.

01:15:12.595 --> 01:15:14.095
- People love you.

01:15:15.450 --> 01:15:17.471
- Thank you so much.

01:15:17.471 --> 01:15:18.304
Thank you.

01:15:19.821 --> 01:15:21.571
Thank you, thank you.

01:15:23.914 --> 01:15:25.664
Thank you, thank you.

01:15:28.630 --> 01:15:30.951
- And there's a lovely reception

01:15:30.951 --> 01:15:33.550
that is gonna be outside
in the U-AG lobby.

01:15:33.550 --> 01:15:34.920
Please feel free to join us.

01:15:34.920 --> 01:15:37.088
It is open to all of you.

01:15:37.088 --> 01:15:39.150
You've been a wonderful audience

01:15:39.150 --> 01:15:41.403
and this is our way of thanking you.

01:15:41.403 --> 01:15:42.525
So, thank you.

01:15:42.525 --> 01:15:43.525
- Thank you.

01:17:58.518 --> 01:18:00.935
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

